---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

// PLACEHOLDER: this is a working draft, not legal advice. Costa Rican rental
// law and liability terms should be reviewed by a local attorney before this
// page is relied on for protection — flagged the same way in chat.
// The cancellation policy below is deliberately non-committal because no
// specific cancellation terms have been confirmed with the owner yet.
const lastUpdated = 'August 27, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms &amp; Conditions | Rent ATV Santa Teresa"
  description="Booking, payment, deposit, delivery and liability terms for ATV rentals arranged through Rent ATV Santa Teresa."
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Terms & Conditions', href: '/terms-and-conditions' }]} />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms &amp; Conditions"
    subtitle={`Last updated ${lastUpdated} — please read before booking`}
  />

  <section class="page-x pt-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl rounded-media bg-surface p-6">
      <p class="text-base font-semibold text-ink-2">Our role, in short</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-muted">
        Rent ATV Santa Teresa is a booking and coordination service. We
        connect riders with independently owned and operated local ATV
        vendors in the Santa Teresa area — we do not own, manufacture, or
        directly maintain the vehicles ourselves. Each rental is provided and
        equipped by the local operator we match you with. See "Our role" below
        for what this means for you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-x section-y">
    <div class="prose-content max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Our role</h2>
      <p>
        Rent ATV Santa Teresa acts as a booking service connecting visitors
        with independent, locally owned and operated ATV rental vendors
        ("Partner Vendors") in and around Santa Teresa, Costa Rica. When you
        book through us, your rental agreement for the vehicle itself is with
        the Partner Vendor who supplies it — not with Rent ATV Santa Teresa
        directly. We coordinate the booking, delivery, pricing and
        communication on your behalf, and our Partner Vendors are responsible
        for the condition, maintenance and roadworthiness of their own
        vehicles.
      </p>

      <h2>Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        To rent an ATV you must be at least 18 years old and hold a valid
        driver's licence from your home country — a standard car licence is
        enough. Bring the physical card; a photo on your phone is not
        accepted.
      </p>

      <h2>Bookings &amp; payment</h2>
      <p>
        Bookings are made by messaging us on WhatsApp with your dates, number
        of riders and where you are staying. Nothing is charged when you
        reserve. Payment — in cash (Costa Rican colones or US dollars) or by
        card — is due at pickup. Rates are listed on our{' '}
        <a href="/pricing" class="link-inline">pricing page</a> and drop the
        longer you rent.
      </p>

      <h2>Security deposit</h2>
      <p>
        A security deposit starting from $500, held on card or in cash, is
        required at pickup and refunded on return, less the cost of any
        damage beyond normal wear. The exact amount depends on the quad you
        rent.
      </p>

      <h2>Delivery &amp; collection</h2>
      <p>
        We deliver free of charge within Santa Teresa, Mal País, Playa Carmen
        and Playa Hermosa. Delivery to Cóbano or Cabuya carries an extra fee.
        Message us your accommodation and we will confirm timing and any
        applicable fee.
      </p>

      <h2>Assumption of risk</h2>
      <p>
        Riding an ATV is an inherently hazardous activity, made more so by
        Santa Teresa's unpaved, uneven and sometimes muddy roads. By renting,
        you acknowledge this risk and agree that you ride at your own risk.
        Neither Rent ATV Santa Teresa nor the Partner Vendor supplying your
        vehicle can guarantee your safety, and both disclaim liability for
        injury, death or property damage to the fullest extent permitted
        under Costa Rican law, except where caused by the Partner Vendor's own
        gross negligence.
      </p>

      <h2>Rider responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Wear the helmet provided at all times while riding.</li>
        <li>Hold a valid licence and carry it with you.</li>
        <li>Obey Costa Rican traffic law and posted signage.</li>
        <li>Never ride on protected beach sections or through nesting areas.</li>
        <li>Avoid riding after dark — the coast road is unlit.</li>
        <li>Do not operate the ATV under the influence of alcohol or drugs.</li>
        <li>Carry no more than one passenger, and only on a two-seater model.</li>
        <li>Do not lend the ATV to anyone not named on the rental agreement.</li>
        <li>You are personally responsible for any traffic fines or penalties incurred during your rental.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Vehicle condition</h2>
      <p>
        Each ATV is provided by the Partner Vendor who owns it, and that
        vendor is responsible for its mechanical condition, servicing and
        roadworthiness. If you believe a vehicle is unsafe at pickup, tell us
        immediately and do not ride it — we will arrange a replacement or a
        refund of amounts not yet used.
      </p>

      <h2>Insurance &amp; damage</h2>
      <p>
        Basic liability coverage is included with every rental, arranged
        through the Partner Vendor; ask us about its limits before you sign.
        Optional damage cover is available for a daily fee and reduces what
        you are liable for if the ATV is returned damaged. Where damage cover
        is not taken, you are responsible for the cost of repairs, up to the
        value of your security deposit and beyond it if repair costs exceed
        that amount.
      </p>

      <h2>Cancellations</h2>
      <p>
        Plans change — message us as soon as you know and we will do what we
        can to move your booking to a new date. Cancellation and refund terms
        are confirmed with you directly on WhatsApp at the time of booking.
      </p>

      <h2>Prohibited use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No racing, stunt riding, or off-roading outside marked trails and roads.</li>
        <li>No modifying the vehicle.</li>
        <li>No use for any illegal purpose.</li>
        <li>No removing or disabling safety equipment.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to be responsible for, and to reimburse Rent ATV Santa
        Teresa and the relevant Partner Vendor for, any loss, fine or claim
        arising from your own negligent, reckless or unlawful use of the ATV,
        to the extent permitted by Costa Rican law.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, Rent ATV Santa Teresa's role
        is limited to coordinating your booking. Any claim relating to the
        ATV itself — its mechanical condition, an accident, or an injury
        arising from its use — should be directed to the Partner Vendor who
        supplied the vehicle and, where applicable, their insurance. Rent ATV
        Santa Teresa is not liable for indirect, incidental or consequential
        damages arising from your rental.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of Costa Rica. Any dispute will
        be handled in the courts of Puntarenas province.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time; the date at the top
        shows the last revision. Continuing to book with us after a change
        means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Message us on WhatsApp —{' '}
        <a href={`tel:${site.phoneHref}`} class="link-inline">{site.phoneDisplay}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Ready to book?"
    body="Send your dates and how many riders. We reply in minutes during opening hours."
    message="Hi! I have a question before booking an ATV in Santa Teresa."
  />
</BaseLayout>
